============================================== Simulation logic ==============================================

When I click a simulation button of a rule, run simulation for the matched tokens, and show total simulation result above the rules table, simulated tokens list table under the rules table, instead of "Matched tokens table".

Simulation runs like this:

1. my First Entry Price logic
- Just after the token is created and creator buy, there are many other transactions trade this newly created token (like other bots).
- They all have same block timestamp. 
- Let's assume my bot is not so fast to inject in the first block. So let's see about second block. 
- In this second block, maybe from first to fifth transaction can be my first entry transaction. I'll change the transaction compare lange later.
- So check about these transaction histories of the token, and the highest buy price will be my first entry price.
- The highest price is from first block and 1-5 transactions of second block.
- The transaction signature of the highest price will be my first entry transaction.

2. my Exit Entry Price logic
- Similar with First Entry Price logic.
- When a transaction meets the "take profit"/"stop loss", calculate the exit entry price
- In that block, the lowest token price will be my Exit Entry Price.
- The transaction signature of the lowest price will be my exit entry transactio.

3. Show in simulated tokens result table under the rules table
- For each tokens matched with the selected rule, find the entry, exit transactions according to above logics.
- Calculate the PnL, holding time, etc.
- Show token simulated result data like rule name, token symbol, entry price(SOL), entry time, exit price(SOL), exit time, PnL, holding time, exit reason, TP/SL, PnL SOL in a row.

4. Display a total simulation result on top of rules table
